    <fr:title text="Group Homomorphism">Group Homomorphism</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
Let <fr:tex display="inline">(G,\times )</fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline">(H,\circ )</fr:tex> be groups. A map <fr:tex display="inline">\phi  : G\to  H</fr:tex> such that
<fr:tex display="inline">\forall  x,y\in  G,\phi (x\times  y)=\phi (x)\circ \phi (y)</fr:tex> is called a <html:strong>group homomorphism</html:strong>.
</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
